      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nInterested in this property? \nSign up for mySherryFitz to arrange your viewing, see current offers or make your own offer. Register now at SherryFitz.ie\n\n4 / 5 Bedroom Detached House c. 169.58 sqm. in the popular village of Newtownforbes just off the N4 Dublin Road convenient to Longford Town, local shops and amenities.\n\nThe house was originally built in 2008 to a high standard and is presented in excellent walk in condition. The house features a large sitting room with wooden floors a bay window and an open fireplace. This room opens into the rear living room that has a glass door out to the rear garden. This room is south east facing ensuring a bright room throughout the early part of the day. \n\nThe kitchen is spacious has built in units and appliances with polished stone worktops. The kitchen is complimented by a utility room that is plumbed for a washing machine and dryer that also accesses the rear with a WC off this. The kitchen opens into the dining room area that has wooden floors and built in display units. \n\nUpstairs the main bedroom is spacious and has an ensuite shower room. The remaining 3 bedrooms are all double sized and are served by a family bathroom, that has a separate shower. There is a study / office that could be used a single sized bedroom, but would make an ideal home office taking advantage of the fibre to the home broadband available here.\n\n\nServices :\n• Mains Water and Sewerage, \n• Oil fired central heating \n• Fibre to the home high speed broadband.\n\n\nOutside :\nThe rear of the house has a south east facing aspect and has a patio area and lawn with mature planting and a wooden garden shed. To the front of the house there is a large tarmac driveway with parking space for a number of cars. \n\n\nLocation :\nThe house is located just off the N4 Dublin Sligo Road, easy walking distance to the local shops & pubs. Newtownforbes takes its name from the Forbes family, also known as the Earl of Granard, and have been resident in Castleforbes since 1691.\n \nNewtownforbes is a popular residential location with an excellent Primary school, and modern GAA complex, which the house is very close to. The village has local shops, post office, restaurant and churches. Being on the N4 Dublin Sligo Road there are bus stops along the main street and Longford town centre is just a 5 minute drive. The village has an active tidy town group and recently helped develop a heritage & biodiversity trail walk that is convenient to the house.\n\n\nDirections:\nEircode: N39 AK18 \nGPS: 53.7628, -7.8311"
      },
